  "articleBody": "Exterior door jambs take heavy abuse from splashback, melting snow, and blocked roof gutters. While it is tempting to spread exterior wood filler over peeling paint or rotted jamb bases, cosmetic patches never resolve underlying water intrusion. Over time, moisture wicks upward into structural jack studs and the garage header.\n\nSigns You Need Structural Frame Repair:\nLook for doors that bind against the track during cold snaps, diagonal drywall cracks radiating from the upper corners of the opening, or a visible sag along the horizontal header beam. If pressing a screwdriver into the bottom four inches of the wood jamb yields soft, spongy fiber, moisture has penetrated behind the exterior trim.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice:\nWhen rot is confined strictly to the exterior brick mold, simple trim replacement and proper aluminum flashing may solve the issue. However, if the jamb supports track brackets or the header has settled under the weight of the roof or living space above, the opening must be temporarily shored while deteriorated structural lumber is rebuilt to plumb.\n\nWhat to Do Next:\nNever attach high-tension garage components to soft wood. For complete garage door frame and structural header repairs across the Denver area, get in touch with Abraham at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
